---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header";
import Footer from "../components/Footer";
import KeyboardTestLauncher from "../components/KeyboardTestLauncher";

const title = "Keyboard Tester Online – Test All Keys & Numpad | GOATTYPE";
const description = "Launch GOATTYPE's free fullscreen keyboard tester for letters, F1–F12, arrows, navigation keys, number pad, ghosting, rollover, and missing keys.";
const canonicalPath = "/keyboard-test/";
const faqItems = [
  ["How can I test whether my keyboard is working properly?", "Select Launch keyboard test, then press every physical key in the fullscreen tester. Working keys light up and remain marked. Press Escape or End test to return to the guide."],
  ["Does the keyboard tester open another page?", "No. The tester opens as a fullscreen experience over the current keyboard-test page. Closing it returns you to the same guide, header, content, and footer."],
  ["How do I exit the keyboard test?", "Press the Escape key at any time or select the End test button at the top of the tester. Keyboard Lock is released and normal page behavior returns immediately."],
  ["Can the tester stop brightness, volume, screenshot, and other system actions?", "Fullscreen Keyboard Lock can suppress many browser actions where supported, but a website cannot override controls handled directly by device firmware or the operating system."],
  ["Can this keyboard tester check the number pad?", "Yes. It includes Num Lock, divide, multiply, subtract, add, Enter, decimal, and number-pad digits 0 through 9."],
  ["How do I test F1–F12?", "Launch the fullscreen test. Compact laptops may also require Fn or Fn Lock. A firmware-handled brightness or media action may not produce a browser event."],
  ["Can a keyboard tester detect ghosting?", "It can reveal practical ghosting or rollover limits. Hold several keys together and compare the highlighted keys with the Held now counter."],
  ["Does the keyboard test record what I type?", "No. Detection runs locally in the browser and the page does not save your keystrokes."],
];
const structuredData = [
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebApplication", name: "GOATTYPE Online Keyboard Tester", url: "https://typeittestit.com/keyboard-test/", applicationCategory: "UtilityApplication", operatingSystem: "Any", description, featureList: ["Fullscreen 104-key test", "Function-key testing", "Numeric keypad testing", "Keyboard Lock", "Ghosting and rollover check"], offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "USD" } },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", mainEntity: faqItems.map(([name, text]) => ({ "@type": "Question", name, acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text } })) },
];
---
<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath={canonicalPath} structuredData={structuredData}>
  <div class="relative min-h-screen">
    <Header client:idle />
    <main>
      <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pb-14 pt-20 sm:px-6 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-28 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr]">
          <div>
            <p class="font-label uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Free browser diagnostic</p>
            <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl font-heading-1 text-ink">Test every key in one focused fullscreen tool</h1>
            <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-body-lg text-text-muted">Launch the complete 104-key tester directly from this page. It opens fullscreen, begins capturing immediately, and returns you to this guide when you press Escape or choose End test.</p>
            <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4"><KeyboardTestLauncher client:load /><a href="#how-it-works" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas px-7 py-3.5 font-link text-ink transition-colors hover:border-text-muted">How it works</a></div>
            <p class="mt-4 font-caption text-text-faint">No second page. Press Esc at any time to close the test and restore normal keyboard behavior.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-[28px] border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-7 shadow-sm sm:p-9">
            <p class="font-label uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">What happens after launch</p>
            <ol class="mt-6 space-y-4 font-body text-text-muted"><li><strong class="text-ink">1.</strong> The keyboard tester fills the screen.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">2.</strong> Keyboard capture and supported Keyboard Lock start automatically.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">3.</strong> Pressed keys light up and stay marked.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">4.</strong> Press Esc or End test to return here.</li></ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <article id="how-it-works" class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-16 border-t border-hairline px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-8">
        <section><p class="font-label uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-accent">Complete guide</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-heading-3 text-ink">How the GOATTYPE keyboard tester works</h2><div class="mt-7 grid gap-8 font-body text-text-muted md:grid-cols-2"><div class="space-y-4"><p>The browser produces a <code class="text-ink">keydown</code> event when a physical key is pressed and a <code class="text-ink">keyup</code> event when it is released. GOATTYPE reads the physical <code class="text-ink">KeyboardEvent.code</code> to match that position with the visual keyboard.</p><p>The physical code distinguishes left and right Shift, Control, Alt, and Meta keys. The browser key value may change with Shift, Caps Lock, Num Lock, language settings, or remapping.</p></div><div class="space-y-4"><p>A bright key is currently held. A softly marked key has registered at least once. Untested keys remain neutral, and the progress meter shows how much of the full-size layout has been checked.</p><p>The test confirms that an event reached the webpage. It cannot electrically inspect the switch, matrix, cable, wireless radio, firmware, or system driver.</p></div></div></section>

        <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12"><h2 class="font-heading-3 text-ink">One page, one launch action</h2><div class="mt-7 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Launch here</h3><p class="mt-4 font-body text-text-muted">The footer link opens this complete GOATTYPE page with its normal header, guide, FAQ, and footer. The Launch button starts the tool without navigating elsewhere.</p></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Test fullscreen</h3><p class="mt-4 font-body text-text-muted">The tester covers the viewport and requests browser fullscreen plus Keyboard Lock when supported. Instructions for ending the session remain visible at the top.</p></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Return instantly</h3><p class="mt-4 font-body text-text-muted">Press Escape anywhere in the active tester or choose End test. The overlay closes, Keyboard Lock is released, and this same page reappears at the previous position.</p></div></div></section>

        <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12"><h2 class="font-heading-3 text-ink">Complete testing procedure</h2><ol class="mt-7 grid gap-5 font-body text-text-muted md:grid-cols-2"><li class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><strong class="text-ink">1. Prepare the keyboard.</strong><br />Connect it directly, charge wireless models, choose the intended language, and turn Num Lock on.</li><li class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><strong class="text-ink">2. Launch fullscreen testing.</strong><br />Select Launch keyboard test. Capture begins automatically—there is no additional start button.</li><li class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><strong class="text-ink">3. Work section by section.</strong><br />Test letters, number row, punctuation, modifiers, F1–F12, navigation, arrows, and every numpad key.</li><li class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><strong class="text-ink">4. Repeat suspicious input.</strong><br />Reset and press a delayed, missing, sticking, or double-registering key repeatedly.</li><li class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><strong class="text-ink">5. Test combinations.</strong><br />Hold real shortcuts or gaming combinations and compare highlighted keys with Held now.</li><li class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><strong class="text-ink">6. End safely.</strong><br />Press Escape or End test. Confirm any failure in another browser or application.</li></ol></section>

        <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12"><h2 class="font-heading-3 text-ink">Function keys, media controls, and Fn Lock</h2><div class="mt-6 grid gap-8 font-body text-text-muted md:grid-cols-2"><div class="space-y-4"><p>Laptops often combine F1–F12 with brightness, volume, microphone mute, lighting, airplane mode, and playback. Depending on Action Keys or Fn Lock, the traditional function key may require holding Fn.</p><p>If a key changes brightness but F7 does not highlight, the switch may still work—the firmware may have consumed the action before the browser received it. Try Fn plus the key and inspect the event code.</p></div><div class="space-y-4"><p>Print Screen, power, sleep, fingerprint, Touch ID, and protected shortcuts are intentionally difficult or impossible for webpages to suppress. Their behavior varies by device and operating system.</p><p>This restriction prevents malicious pages from trapping essential escape, privacy, power, security, or accessibility controls.</p></div></div></section>

        <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12"><h2 class="font-heading-3 text-ink">Numpad, ghosting, and rollover</h2><div class="mt-6 grid gap-8 font-body text-text-muted md:grid-cols-2"><div><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Number-pad behavior</h3><p class="mt-3">The tester includes keypad 0–9, decimal, operators, Num Lock, and Enter. With Num Lock disabled, some systems report keypad positions as Home, End, Insert, Delete, Page Up, Page Down, or arrows.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Multi-key testing</h3><p class="mt-3">Ghosting occurs when the keyboard matrix cannot report a combination correctly. Hold combinations used for games, shortcuts, or fast typing and compare the highlights with the simultaneous-key counter.</p></div></div></section>

        <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12"><h2 class="font-heading-3 text-ink">Troubleshooting by keyboard type</h2><div class="mt-7 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Laptop</h3><p class="mt-4 font-body text-text-muted">Restart, check Fn Lock and Filter Keys, update manufacturer utilities, and test before login. Adjacent rows failing together may indicate a ribbon-cable or matrix fault.</p></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">USB or mechanical</h3><p class="mt-4 font-body text-text-muted">Try another cable and port, avoid unpowered hubs, disable remapping profiles, and compare on a second computer.</p></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6"><h3 class="font-heading-5 text-ink">Bluetooth or wireless</h3><p class="mt-4 font-body text-text-muted">Recharge batteries, pair again, move closer to the receiver, reduce radio interference, and test through a cable if supported.</p></div></div></section>

        <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12"><h2 class="font-heading-3 text-ink">Layouts, cleaning, and repair</h2><div class="mt-6 grid gap-8 font-body text-text-muted md:grid-cols-2"><div class="space-y-4"><p>The diagram follows a common 104-key ANSI layout. ISO, JIS, Apple, regional, ergonomic, compact, and tenkeyless keyboards may move, omit, or layer keys.</p><p>Power down before cleaning. Use compressed air at an angle and a lightly dampened cloth. Never spray liquid directly onto a keyboard or force laptop scissor keycaps.</p></div><div class="space-y-4"><p>Seek repair when a key fails across devices or applications, several keys in one row stop together, input occurs without touching the keyboard, or liquid entered the device.</p><p>After confirming the hardware works, continue with the <a href="/#tester" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">GOATTYPE typing speed test</a>.</p></div></div></section>
      </article>

      <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl border-t border-hairline px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-8" aria-labelledby="keyboard-faq-heading"><p class="font-label uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-accent">Keyboard troubleshooting</p><h2 id="keyboard-faq-heading" class="mt-3 font-heading-3 text-ink">Keyboard Tester FAQ</h2><div class="mt-8 divide-y divide-hairline border-y border-hairline">{faqItems.map(([question, answer]) => <details class="group py-1"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-5 font-heading-5 text-ink marker:content-none"><span>{question}</span><span class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-hairline text-text-muted transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p class="max-w-4xl pb-6 pr-12 font-body text-text-muted">{answer}</p></details>)}</div><div class="mt-10"><KeyboardTestLauncher client:visible label="Launch fullscreen test" /></div></section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
